    "body": "Great proposal 🙌 Would be very cool to see something like this in the web platform.\n\n> To workaround this, the following are common on the web platform today:\n\nDoes it make sense to also add another point to the common web platform patterns?\n\n- Send the user's time zone to the server\n  - Does not work with statically rendered HTML\n  - Passive client hint could be used for fingerprinting\n\nfrom prior art like this:\n\n- https://github.com/epicweb-dev/client-hints (also https://github.com/epicweb-dev/epic-stack/discussions/307)\n- https://web.archive.org/web/20251108132906/https://www.jacobparis.com/content/remix-ssr-dates\n- https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/38263#discussioncomment-3084482\n- standards proposal https://github.com/romulocintra/user-locale-client-hints#proposed-solution",
    "author_association": "NONE",
