    "updated_at": "2026-06-22T09:04:43Z",
    "body": "On `hour12` vs. `hourCycle`, here's a good summary of how/why we ended up with only the former in Unicode MessageFormat: https://github.com/unicode-org/message-format-wg/issues/1097#issuecomment-3188558284\n\nThe short answer is that h24 is not actually used by any locale (and might even get deprecated, see https://github.com/tc39/ecma402/issues/1002), and that the choice between h11 and h12 is locale-dependent. This leaves the true/false/undefined values of `hour12` as the three options that we do actively want to support, and the option name \"hour12\" as the least worst option we've come across so far. Recommendations are quite welcome for improvements; https://github.com/unicode-org/message-format-wg/issues/1097 is probably the best place for such.\n\nThe specifics of `timeZone` and its `input` value are documented [here](https://github.com/unicode-org/message-format-wg/blob/main/spec/functions/datetime.md#date-and-time-override-options).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
