    "body": "> > To workaround this, the following are common on the web platform today:\n> \n> Does it make sense to also add another point to the common web platform patterns?\n> \n>     * Send the user's time zone to the server\n>       \n>       * Does not work with statically rendered HTML\n>       * Passive client hint could be used for fingerprinting\n\nWhile I assume this is proposed with good intentions, it seems it would likely just end up as yet another data-point to be exploited by data-brokers. I much prefer OP's purely client-side solution.\n",
