    "created_at": "2026-06-23T18:40:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-23T18:40:09Z",
    "body": "@andreas-taranetz This is a supported use case already! What you can do is provide a stringified `Temporal.ZonedDateTime` in `datetime`, which includes a timezone such as `Europe/Amsterdam` (e.g. `2026-06-23T20:37:07.255570068+02:00[Europe/Amsterdam]`). By default, this would be converted to the user's local timezone and displayed. However, when you specify `timezone=input`, it will instead be displayed in the timezone specified inside the `ZonedDateTime` string. This option is only supported for `ZonedDateTime` strings. Example:\n\n```html\n<time datetime=\"2026-06-23T20:37:07.255570068+02:00[Europe/Amsterdam]\" format=\"datetime\" timezone=\"input\">fallback</time>\n```\n\nThis matches the behaviour of `:datetime` in Message Format 2.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
